Essay: *El escritor argentino y la tradición*, 1932, repr. 1951 in *Otras inquisiciones / Other Inquisitions*, “The Argentine Writer and the Tradition”. 

The parenthesis *las ilusiones del patriotismo no tienen fin / the illusions of patriotism have no end* is illustrated in the editorial tradition that is most widely reproduced with the canonical Greek–English–German national self-panegyric topos:

* Greek panegyric *es cosa grande ser griego / a great thing is to be a Greek* – Pindar;
* English Victorian patriotic panegyric on England – Lord Thomas Babington Macaulay, *History of England*;
* German patriotic panegyric – Johann Gottlieb Fichte, *Reden an die deutsche Nation*.

Pindar, Thomas Babington Macaulay, Johann Gottlieb Fichte

